use ../../../lib/UiComponent

from ../../../behaviors/Presence import Presence
from ../Collapsible import Collapsible

export ui-component Accordion:
    description:
        An accordion is a stack of sections, each with a heading the user can
        press to show or hide what's under it, like a list of frequently asked
        questions. It saves space on a page with a lot to read.

    composes:
        - @{Collapsible}

    behaviors:
        - @{Presence}

    headings:
        Each section's trigger sits inside a heading at the right level for
        the page, so assistive tools can list and jump between sections the
        same way as other headings. The trigger tells assistive tools whether
        its section is shown.

    expansion:
        The component decides whether only one section can be open at a time
        or several. With one at a time, opening a section closes whichever was
        open before. With several, each opens and closes on its own.

    collapsing:
        With several allowed, any open section can be closed. With one at a
        time, the component decides whether the open section can be closed
        again, leaving every section closed, or whether one must always stay
        open.

    keyboard:
        Every trigger is its own stop in the Tab order, because the open
        sections between them may hold things to Tab to. As well as that, the
        Up and Down arrow keys move between triggers, and Home and End go to
        the first and last. Whether the arrow keys wrap around at the ends is
        up to the chosen library.

    orientation:
        Sections are usually stacked top to bottom. They can also sit side by
        side, and then Left and Right move between triggers instead, reversed
        for right-to-left languages.

    disabled:
        A section can be disabled, and so can the whole accordion. A disabled
        section can't be opened or closed by the user, and the arrow keys pass
        over its trigger.

    reporting:
        The component is told which sections are open whenever that changes,
        and can open or close sections itself.

    nonGoals:
        - Not tabs. Tabs always show exactly one panel in the same place
        - Not for a single section. That's a Collapsible
        - No dragging sections to reorder them
